{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:0.1"], "en": "The Questions of King Milinda,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:0.2"], "en": "Great Chapter 7:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:0.3"], "en": "The Question on Wise Attention (Yonisomanasikāra)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:1.1"], "en": "The King said:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:1.2"], "en": "\"Venerable Nāgasena, he who does not undergo rebirth—does he not fail to undergo rebirth because of wise attention?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:1.3"], "en": "\"Both through wise attention, Great King, and through wisdom and other wholesome states,\" [replied Nāgasena].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:1.4"], "en": "“But, venerable sir, is not wise attention itself wisdom?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:1.5"], "en": "“No, great king; attention is one thing, wisdom is another. For even goats, sheep, oxen, buffaloes, camels, and donkeys have attention, yet they do not possess wisdom.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:2.1"], "en": "“You are clever, venerable Nāgasena.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_mil_3.1.7:3.1"], "en": "The seventh inquiry: On Appropriate Attention.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:59:40Z"}
]
